ginan-iers2010 (libgnss++ vendored subset)
==========================================

This directory contains C++ wrappers around IERS Conventions (2010)
routines, adapted from:

    Geoscience Australia - Ginan
    https://github.com/GeoscienceAustralia/ginan
    Copyright 2020 Geoscience Australia
    Licensed under Apache License, Version 2.0

The wrapper code is itself a translation/wrapper of FORTRAN routines
distributed by the IERS as part of the IERS Conventions 2010 software:

    https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/

The IERS Conventions 2010 routines are public-domain scientific software
produced under the auspices of the International Earth Rotation and
Reference Systems Service. The C++ wrappers in this directory are
licensed under Apache License, Version 2.0 (see ./LICENSE).

A list of modifications made by libgnss++ to the upstream ginan sources
is recorded in ./README.md ("Modifications" section), as required by
Apache License 2.0 §4(b).

Rust translation in gnss-rust
============================
Derived from libgnss++ commit 72f3b7c2c4c088dc575286a6f0edf4e407bc499a,
third_party/ginan-iers2010/dehanttideinel/dehanttide_all.cpp.
Underlying Ginan source: GeoscienceAustralia/ginan@535ef0a (v4.1.1).

src/iers2010.rs is a Rust translation with these modifications:
- Fixed arrays replace Eigen vectors; API evaluates one station per call.
- Explicit TT-century/UT-hour arguments and Earth-fixed Sun/Moon inputs.
- Input and result validation, including errors on axial stations rather
  than division by zero, and errors instead of nonfinite displacements.
- Body terms share scalar expressions; return individual correction terms
  and instantaneous coordinates as well as the summed displacement.
- Step-1 and Step-2 retained; no permanent-tide Step-3 added.
No SOFA source is included in the Rust library.
